{
  "about": "Router v10's eval set (lib/ai/ask.ts AskFiltersV10). One GET /api/ask per question with the x-ask-eval header (eval-howto in the stage notes; grade.mjs grades the saved replies). `expect`: the reading's fields that must match, read from the reply's memo (the filters it sends back for follow-ups) and its intent; v10's fields are snake_case as in the schema. `facts`: what the answer must respect, checked by grade.mjs against the reply's cards, games and words, and against truth.json (the claimed set, players' reports and stars, the owner's prices as the turf page shows them, read SELECT-only from the database, and each turf's hours, added by hours-truth.mjs) when one is given. `city`: the visitor's city (?city=); `lat`/`lng`: their location; `ctx`: the page they are on. Free hours (lib/ask/freeHours.ts): free_* questions read the owners' marked free hours; truth.json's free is the turfs whose free hours players see when the replies are saved (SELECT jsonb_path_query_array(public.free_slots_now(), '$.turfs[*].id')), and expect free_hours reads the memo. Tournaments (lib/ask/tournament.ts): tournament-* questions are asked on a tournament's page; `tournament` names one of the three fixture tournaments in lib/ask/tournament.fixtures.ts (league: mid-way, two matches scored live, one typed, one on now; cup: finished, with semi-finals and a final; typed: typed results only), whose page code a runner puts in ctx as {tournament: code}. expect.kind is the usual question it must be read as (other: the model phrases the facts, scripts/ask-eval/tournament-model.json standing in for it offline). npm run test:ask runs them offline through the route's own reading and grades them with grade.mjs (lib/ask/tournament.test.ts).",
